ENTRY {"seat": "codex", "phase": "research", "d": "✓", "date": "2026-09-07", "grade": "CONFIRMED", "outcome": "mte-depth-table", "grader": "main-loop", "ev": "regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/codex_scope_20260907.txt", "note": "INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION of both directions of this row, plus the piece it did not have: **the MTE depth mapping, derived from the live code rather than from `#509`'s comment.**\n\n    MTE depth (bits)   helper colour type   helper bufdepth   unassigned bytes transmitted\n     8                  CI                   1                 0\n    16                  CI                   2                 1\n    32                  RGBA                 4                 0\n    64                  CI                   8                 7\n\n*** THIS IS A LIVE CONSEQUENCE FOR `#509`, WHICH SHIPPED TODAY. ***  `#509` repaired the RGBA selection at depth 32 and that repair is confirmed present.  But the tiled MTE path still constructs **CI at bufdepth 2 and bufdepth 8**, and CI assigns only `buf[0]` -- so MTE transfers at 16 and 64 bits transmit 1 and 7 uninitialised host-stack bytes respectively.  `#509` was correct and scoped to the 32-bit cell by its own comment; this row owns the remainder, and the depth table is what makes the remainder concrete rather than hypothetical.\n\nThe full PUT initialisation census, which supersedes any per-arm reasoning:\n\n    PUT arm          bytes assigned   depths transmitting unassigned bytes\n    CI                     1          2, 4, 8  ->  1, 3, 7 unassigned\n    RGB/RGBA/ABGR          4          8        ->  4 unassigned\n    default (random)       4          8        ->  4 unassigned\n\nAnd the callee question is closed: `memcpy(memblock + offset, data, len)` copies the requested length; block-boundary crossings split 
