ENTRY {"seat": "opus5", "phase": "assess", "d": "HELD", "date": "2026-09-08", "grade": "HELD", "outcome": "", "grader": "main-loop", "ev": "regress/artifacts/alphatbinegsel/panel_assess_20260908/", "hold_question": "BUILD THE WITNESS.  You are the compile-and-measure seat and this row's single unvalidated element is its witness -- codex's own status line was 'source-confirmed functional defect; witness UNVALIDATED', and an earlier draft of my packet compressed that to 'verified', which the assess panel caught.  The design: on unmodified -E alpha -e alphabook1, fill a mapping, remap the PTE behind it, call ALPHA_TBIA(), then load and observe the OLD value.  *** THE TRAP: the debugger ALL-FLUSHES between interactions, so the fill, remap, tbi and observing load must be inside ONE step N or both builds re-walk and the row is GREEN on the defective build.  And K0SEG is checked BEFORE ptbr, so a K0SEG address never consults the page table and cannot witness this at all. ***  THREE CHANNELS THE ASSESS PANEL SAID IT MAY MISS, each owed a row or a disclosure: (a) kimi -- a same-VA STORE then load reads back green on a broken build; (b) kimi -- permission-only remaps; (c) deepseek -- the row is VACUOUS when the old and new data happen to match, so the remap must change the observed BYTES and not merely the mapping.  Report pre-fix RED and post-fix GREEN with the same script, or say plainly that you could not build it and what stopped you.  *** TWO MORE VACUITY TRAPS, from the agy seat, and the FIRST is the one this row's own design walks into: (d) DO NOT USE VPN 0 AS THE TEST PAGE.  HEAD's defective arm flushes page zero, so a witness on page 0 goes GREEN ON THE DEFECTIVE BUILD -- the defect is that only page 0 is flushed, so page 0 is the one page that cannot witness it.  (e) ZERO a1 
