ENTRY {"seat": "fable5", "phase": "design", "d": "2026-09-09", "date": "2026-09-09", "note": "ADJUDICATED BY THE MAIN LOOP RUNNING AS FABLE 5.1 (owner directive 2026-09-09: \"proceed with fable for any adjudication\").  This is the adjudicator hat, not an independent seat review; it is recorded as fable5 because that is the seat the hold names.  RULING on the three questions.  (1) YES -- MEASURE the width-32 lowering BEFORE shipping.  codex's warning is the 'definedness repair hiding a behaviour correction' shape exactly, and the manual is LOCAL: ddi0406.txt:18066 (A8.8.20) makes width 32 copy the whole register.  If the OLD count-masked host shift made the mask zero at width 32, the fix CHANGES guest-visible behaviour and the round must SAY so with a ROW -- CLAIM -> ROW is not optional.  One row.  (2) PRESERVE SILENTLY, with a comment citing A8.8.20: UNPREDICTABLE mandates nothing, so preserve is a policy choice; the addition licence forbids an announce with no measured delta; and the house latched announce is for guest-drivable DEFECTS -- an UNPREDICTABLE encoding is not one.  (3) The detector may claim the WIDTH axis at the value level (32 and <= 0) and may NOT claim a `1U' -> `1' regression -- that is `ubsanshiftlane' debt, a different tool class (sanitizer or source pin), and it does NOT have to land first: #510 shipped under the same disclosure, and the reopening rule says more witnesses make more rounds, not bigger ones.", "grader": "main-loop (Fable 5.1)", "grade": "RULING", "ev": "_scratchpad/ddi0406.txt:18066"}
