Footbridge still has eight guest-access exits, including a read whose return value is already computed. I also confirmed that the Alpha VM exit is confined to the supervisor bootstrap path with a zero page-table base. I’m weighing those host exits against silent data errors and checking whether proposed “easy” work would close a whole row.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "@'
import re,sys,subprocess
from pathlib import Path
sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')
lex=re.compile(r'/\\*.*?\\*/|//["'^'"\\n]*|\"(?:\\\\.|["'^"'"\\\\])*\"|\\x27(?:\\\\.|["'^'"\\x27\\\\])*\\x27',re.S)
for p in sorted(Path('src/devices').glob('*.c')):
 s=subprocess.check_output(['git','show','1ce8296:'+p.as_posix()]).decode('utf-8',errors='replace')
 clean=lex.sub(lambda m: ''.join('\\n' if c=='\\n' else ' ' for c in m.group()),s)
 lines=s.splitlines(); hits=[]
 for m in re.finditer(r'\\bexit\\(1\\)',clean):
  n=s.count('\\n',0,m.start())+1
  hits.append(n)
 if not hits: continue
 print('\\nFILE',p.as_posix())
 for n in hits:
  print(n, ' / '.join(line.strip() for line in lines[max(0,n-5):n+1]))
