Two distinctions are clear now: `sgirebufuninit` still moves partially initialized pixel data, so the later RGB repair did not close it; and `n6` is not a one-edit closure, even though one of its eight sites is small. The `lcaisalane` witness now exists in artifacts despite its empty ledger field. Its claim about an uninitialized byte also needs narrowing because the memory layer clears failed-read buffers.
