I opened every top-five site in both tables at `1ce8296`; each listed defect remains.

The “no witness” cost reductions come from actual probe headers and launch code: WDC probes use unmodified Malta and expose a BE leg; SGI RGB/MTE probes use unmodified IP32; ARM uses `testarm`; Alpha probes use `alphabook1`. These provide existing access machinery, **not evidence that the newly proposed observation has already been measured**.

**Reachable exits with no row**

The requested literal line census is **370: devices 241, CPUs 94, machines 35**, identical at HEAD and in the working tree. Git Bash could not start under the sandbox’s Windows restrictions; I obtained the equivalent count with `rg` and an independent immediate-`*.c` Python count.

Removing comments and strings leaves **240 lexical calls at HEAD**, versus **233 in the working tree**; these counts still include disabled code and unreachable guards. The seven-call difference is #518. Its added comments preserve the misleadingly unchanged literal count.

