**Other findings from checking**

- **Dead or unestablished exits must stay out of the reachable total.** The MTE width tail has complementary preceding conditions; GD-ROM clears command-receive state when its count reaches twelve; OSIOP’s outer command switch exhausts its masked domain. The two `m88kexit` branches cannot receive their required status from the current exception paths. PCC2’s unsupported interrupt lines have no current producer. Dyntrans refcount guards and end-of-page assertions remain internal-invariant checks without an established guest-triggered failure here. All **34 executable machine-file exits** inspected are setup/configuration paths.
- **Several candidate-state rows already shipped.** The [CHANGELOG](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/CHANGELOG.md) records `lcaconfbus1kill` **#515**, `alphaswpctxreg` **#514**, the register-read portion of `sgirekills` **#513**, `pcc2c040kill` **#512**, and `sgimtelabelcells` in the **#509 follow-up**. `pcc2widthkills` also shipped its direction split. Older held entries include the `b115` overlay repair **#472**, `wdcrearmzero` **#473**, `fbclearread` **#474**, `wdcnullxfer` **#476**, `wdccdbmidxfer` **#477**, and `sh4tlbda2` **#452**. Remaining coverage or lifecycle debt should not be ranked as the original product defect.
- **`lcaisalane` overstates its initialization claim.** Failed translations and ordinary device reads clear the buffer. The exceptional early halt path can precede clearing, but the outer dispatcher detects CPU stoppage and prevents normal load writeback. The lane error, ignored status, and host exit remain independently real.
- **`alphactxfail` crosses two layers.** `swpctx` ignores store-helper results; the load helpers in `src/core/memory.c` discard read failure themselves. A check only around the current PAL load calls cannot recover status they never return.
- **`armbfcdecode` needs more precise wording.** The decoder passes the backing `r[15]` storage. Calling that value the current PC overstates what this implementation maintains.
